# A push onto a list of numbers that was handed in is one call of a stub, with the list and the bits of the number in registers: the number is not boxed.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="append" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[value]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[bits]] = BitwiseCast(b@[[value]], {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[list]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[length]] = Patchpoint(b@[[list]]:Register({{*}}), b@[[bits]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways{{*}}:CallInline)
# The new length comes back boxed: one test says that it is an integer, and a length of 2^31 or more takes the rare path.
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isInteger]] = AboveEqual(b@[[length]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isInteger]], Terminal, {{*}}:CallInline)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Array.prototype.push cannot be replaced: nothing reads it by name, makes its function object or tests which function it is. There is one call.
# NONE-LABEL: name="append" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: :PropGet
# NONE-NOT: :CallBuiltin
# NONE-COUNT-1: ExitsSideways
# NONE-NOT: ExitsSideways
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# The counts hold a call, whose moves follow the calling convention: not for Windows.
# X64: instructions: 10, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 4
# ARM64: instructions: 9, patchpoints: 1, rare instructions: 4
